From daf82e60c6ea950f3655020bb5577c846af06665 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 21:37:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(daemon): Keep the camera off from PrepareForSleep until
 the resume

- refuse captures between PrepareForSleep(true) and (false): a request admitted in that window has its token cancelled on installation, so an authentication ends cancelled before the camera opens and a preview frame is rejected
- hold a logind delay sleep inhibitor and release it once the camera is closed, retaking it on resume
- clear the sleep gate if the PrepareForSleep stream ends
- record the new suspend rows in ADR 008 and the changelog

The suspend path cancelled the running request and released the camera, but anything admitted afterwards ran. A lock screen locks for the suspend and starts a face scan when the lock is up, which lands in exactly that window, so the camera and IR emitter went into the suspend lit.
