@@ -9,6 +9,15 @@ and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0
 
 ### Fixed
 
+- **The camera and IR emitter no longer go into a suspend lit**: on logind's
+  `PrepareForSleep(true)` the daemon cancelled the running request and released the camera,
+  but a request that arrived after that was admitted. A lock screen that locks for the
+  suspend and starts a face scan once the lock is up landed exactly there, so the camera
+  opened and the emitter lit about a second before the system slept. Captures are now
+  refused from `PrepareForSleep(true)` until `PrepareForSleep(false)` (an authentication
+  ends `cancelled` before the camera opens, a preview frame is rejected), and the daemon
+  holds a logind `delay` sleep inhibitor that it releases once the camera is closed, so the
+  suspend no longer races the release.
 - **Daemon `Authenticate` accepts user-manager callers and checks root callers** (#397):
   with `abort_if_ssh` on (the default), a non-root caller had to belong to a logind session,
   and every process the systemd user manager starts — KDE's `kscreenlocker`, a Quickshell
